  "text": "That's a beautiful intention, Sarah. It takes a lot of courage to share your story, especially when it's about something as personal as mental health. Vulnerability can be scary, but it's also a powerful way to connect with others.\n\nThink about it this way: when you share your story, you're not just talking about your experiences; you're also showing others that they're not alone. You're giving them permission to feel their emotions, to talk about their struggles, and to seek help.\n\nIt's okay to be vulnerable, and it's okay to not have all the answers. In fact, that's often where the most growth happens. You're not expected to have it all figured out; you're expected to be honest, to be real, and to be willing to learn alongside your readers.\n\nRemember, your experiences are valid, and your voice matters. You don't have to be an expert to share your story; you just have to be willing to share it.\n\nHow does that sound? Does that help shift your perspective a bit?",
